WEBVTT

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:24.830
I'm sorry.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.590
But this has to be done.
With your sacrifice,

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.630
our grand plan will become reality.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:38.010
Don't look at me like that.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:40.840
I need to go, so--

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:50.520
You awake?

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.280
What the hell, man? This isn't funny!

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.700
I'm sorry. But this has to be done.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:09.790
With your sacrifice,
our grand plan will become reality.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.790
So...

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.340
I hope you can forgive me,

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.300
Mr. Yellow.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.510
Y-You planned this all along?

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.720
No fair, let me be part...

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.690
of the plan.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:31.690
Let me...

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:43.570
First period, science experiment complete!

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:46.330
Second period... That's Morals class!

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.160
I feel so sorry for him!
I feel so sorry for him!

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.490
That was great!

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:31.670
You should've become a violinist,
not a craftsman here at our shop!

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.590
I like fixing them better.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:37.540
You do?

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:41.130
To my ears,
you play better than most pros!

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.260
Only because of this.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:46.220
Yeah, that's a Gagliano.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:49.970
This was made 300 years ago, wasn't it?

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:53.940
And it wasn't just locked away someplace,
but lovingly used

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:57.810
and kept in good repair,
handed down over the years.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:02.990
I think that's a really amazing thing.

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:07.240
Yeah. If you think about it like that,
it is amazing.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:09.250
How come he's teaching you?

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:12.500
We take a living thing and mend it

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:15.960
so it can be passed down
for another 300 years.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:19.590
It's like the best job in the world.

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:24.720
Even if I die, part of me will live on.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:29.720
Bravo! Well said! You understand deep down
what it is to be a true craftsman!

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:33.190
Unlike my fool of a daughter
who chose to be a detective!

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.430
As my only son, you're my pride!

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.020
Um, I'm your son, Dad.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:38.780
You're dead to me!

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:45.240
Market Maker, a mysterious group
that orchestrates crimes and even wars.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:47.870
Under the orders of the royal family,

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:51.000
they carry out secret activities,
assassinations, sabotage and infiltration.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.960
No individuals, just a collective name.

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:59.000
Its members' right hands are marked
with a skull, although no one's seen it.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.840
It's a mysterious organization
that's gone largely unnoticed in history.

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.130
Is this for real, Kaela?

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:08.390
Hey, wait a minute...

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:14.560
you better not have asked me over here
just to show me this lame, bogus article.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:17.860
Let's go to the crime scene, Bran.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:27.660
Assemblyman Ed Kyle, Personal Residence

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.530
There's little trace evidence.

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:30.490
And over there?

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.410
Mostly wiped down.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:34.300
Where's the Chief?

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.330
He went upstairs a minute ago.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.330
Okay.

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:41.590
What are you doing?

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:44.300
You can't let a civilian
into a crime scene!

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.550
No, ma'am. This is-- Er, sir?

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:51.010
Hey. You're doing that on purpose,
aren't you?

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:52.470
Hey.

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:58.150
Finally back to your old self, I see!

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:06.280
The murdered assemblyman
was always involved in a scandal.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:12.620
He was all over the news recently because
of illegal donations from corporations.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.530
That must be why he was targeted.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:19.040
The arrogant misguided vigilante
scumbag pal again, huh?

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:21.620
Who would do such a thing?

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:24.920
He didn't have to kill the man's family,
too!

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.380
It's "arrogant" now?

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:31.470
It won't stick cause you keep changing it.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:32.380
It was different?

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:33.800
You can't tell?

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:40.770
What's the matter?
Are you feeling sick or something?

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:43.190
This case doesn't involve Killer B.

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:48.740
What are you basing that on?
His usual mark is right there.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:51.990
Keith, what makes you think it wasn't him?

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:54.200
It's sloppy.

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:57.900
Can you explain it to us in simple terms?

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.210
The angles aren't naive.

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:01.740
What is he talking about?

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:04.630
Genie-isms. Basically, I have no idea.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:09.090
Eric, come here a minute.
There's something you should see.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:23.350
Don't get any closer.

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:27.060
Keith, could this be...

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:29.530
Yeah.

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:36.950
This is troublesome.

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:40.160
That it is.

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:44.290
The body in there is definitely dead
as the result of poison gas.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:48.050
Plus, I'm seeing symptoms
of both nerve gas and a blistering agent.

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:55.140
The killer must've created a gas
that combines the properties of each.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:59.480
It's not as fast-acting as nerve gas,
but not as slow as a blistering agent.

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:03.270
Whoever made that stuff is really twisted.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:09.240
It's clear the killer wants his victims
to suffer horribly before he kills them.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:15.570
So, what's the countermeasure?

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:17.620
Simply put, there isn't one.

00:07:19.030 --> 00:07:23.120
If this were an existing gas,
there would be some way to counteract it,

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:25.630
but this is something new,
with refinements added.

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:29.800
I've asked the Army Institute of Medicine
for assistance,

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:34.140
but there's no telling when we'll come up
with an effective counteragent.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.220
In any case, I can't make it here.

00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:42.520
It will be better than nothing, but
all I can do is prepare a preventative.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:44.420
Will it work?

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:45.020
No idea.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:46.860
Come on.

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:50.860
How can I know if something will work
if I haven't made it yet?

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.980
Or would you rather hear the odds?

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:58.120
Not today. If you told me the odds,
I'd probably lose all hope.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:01.700
Personally, I think it's a miracle
that it's not zero.

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:05.950
Spoken like a doctor, same as always.

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:07.250
If you don't like it,

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:11.800
tell Eric to catch the criminal
before he can use the gas.

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.630
Roger that, Doctor.

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:16.420
Genie.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:19.390
Are you still searching?

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:21.970
It's been seven years.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:24.690
Have you learned anything yet?

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:27.350
I still don't know.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:28.640
Then why?

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:33.940
But I have found a clue
that will lead me to the killer.

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:44.160
This is an invitation

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:48.290
to a charity party sent by the mayor
to the murdered assemblyman.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:51.170
A warning he's going to hit the place,
huh?

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:52.760
Any chance it's a bluff?

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:56.220
When we examined the box
left beside the corpse,

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:58.470
albeit a small amount,

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:02.010
we detected real poison gas
in the container inside.

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:06.260
According to the Royal Institute
of Forensic Medicine's report,

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:09.690
it's something new,
and it's highly lethal.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:13.600
If they release something like that
at a party...

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:15.900
It'll affect the entire region.

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:20.370
Depending on weather conditions,
we're looking at millions of deaths.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:25.330
Where did the perp get his hands
on such a nasty gas, anyway?

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:29.290
It's not like
you can just buy it anywhere.

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:34.460
The victim found in the attic
is Ian Reyes. Age, 42. Male.

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:37.760
He was senior researcher
at Premio Farmacia.

00:09:38.170 --> 00:09:42.760
However, he's been missing for six months.
His family even filed a report.

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:45.350
So this guy definitely made the gas.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:48.310
We don't know if it was voluntary
or not, though.

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:50.980
He was eliminated
after he was no longer useful?

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.940
Jonathan, look into Ian Reyes
and his associates.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:55.640
Roger that.

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:59.240
Kaela, contact the relevant ministries
and research agencies.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:02.660
Find out if materials or equipment
used to make poison gas

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.200
-have been reported stolen or missing.
-Yes, sir.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:08.580
Mario and the rest, go to tonight's venue.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:13.090
Check out suspicious people or objects.
Put together a plan to provide security.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.170
Also, to avoid unnecessary panic,

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:19.470
we've been told to keep word of the gas
from the public.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:24.800
I'm not sure if it's even possible
to cover a building this big.

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:27.600
Um, what if this doesn't work?

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:31.440
There are no what-ifs.
If there's no way, we make one.

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:33.520
That's our job.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.470
And now, today's news.

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:09.100
The Royal Police have concluded
that the murders yesterday morning

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:14.520
of Assemblyman Ed Kyle and his family
in their home were the work of Killer B.

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:19.060
An investigation is underway
to learn how the crimes are connected.

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:21.990
-Ow!
-What happened?

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.110
I'm sorry, I nicked myself.

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:26.450
Are you okay?

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:28.580
Wow, it looks pretty deep!

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:32.330
But it doesn't hurt all that much.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:35.120
There.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:42.550
That's a lot of blood.
Have Mother drive you to the hospital.

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:44.210
Honest, I'm fine.

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:48.010
Then go. You don't have to come back.

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:50.350
What? Why are you saying it so coldly?

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:52.060
I didn't mean anything by it!

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:54.000
You're such an obnoxious old fart!

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:54.440
What?
You're such an obnoxious old fart!

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.230
So obnoxious!
I'll be going.

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:57.150
Shut up!

00:11:57.770 --> 00:12:02.070
Legacy Palace

00:12:03.650 --> 00:12:06.870
Charity Ball Venue

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:16.460
-No eating, Lily.
-I won't.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:19.040
-It sounds like it.
-It's physiological.

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:22.880
Don't use that excuse for everything!

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:24.710
Instinct, then.

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:28.100
I'm telling you to do something
about those "instincts."

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:32.560
Over a mic, that doesn't sound like
any noise a human would make!

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.100
It's a distraction!

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:36.980
My mic's in a bad location.

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:15.720
What is that?

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:16.310
An oiran.

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:18.730
That's a classical Japanese outfit.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:23.190
And if that outfit is authentic,
it costs about the same as a Cayenne.

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:24.980
Whoa!

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:28.150
Though to be honest,
I'd take a Hummer over a Cayenne.

00:13:29.690 --> 00:13:32.240
Synchronization complete. We have eyes.

00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:37.780
This is a program that tracks
and analyzes the action curves

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:39.620
of people moving in a crowd.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:45.920
If someone moves against the flow
of traffic or moves abruptly,

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:48.760
it can flag them as suspicious
and track them.

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:51.300
Can it make split-second decisions?

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:52.220
It can.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:57.810
I'm giving you command of the venue.
Do whatever it takes to stop this.

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:01.520
All personnel, report!

00:14:02.350 --> 00:14:04.230
Area one, all clear on this end.

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:06.690
Area two, all clear here, too.

00:14:07.060 --> 00:14:08.200
Ditto.

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:16.540
Keith, Boris, what's your status?

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.380
Building front entrance.

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:30.470
Aside from Keith Flick,
nothing abnormal to report.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:33.180
All search teams,

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:34.600
what's your status?

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:36.430
Area 15, all clear.

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:39.640
Area 16,
no sign of anything here yet, either.

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:42.640
Area 20, all clear.

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:45.690
Area 22, all clear.

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:51.030
Area 24, no sign of any suspicious people
or packages.

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:55.910
Area 27, all clear.

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:58.870
Understood. Continue your search.

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.450
Don't overlook anything.

00:15:01.910 --> 00:15:04.630
The gas ought to be near the HVAC system.

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:08.630
How perceptive of you.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:31.730
Excuse me.

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:52.340
Suspicious person detected!

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:54.260
Venue area 12!

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:57.680
Male, blond hair! The slender waiter!
Heading towards the mayor!

00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:15.700
Suspect apprehended!

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:18.320
Are you all right?

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:19.660
Y Yes.

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:22.620
This man is unharmed, too.

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:26.330
Coming with as crude a weapon as a knife,
huh?

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:29.080
Weren't you going to use "it"?

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:33.960
I was worried sick
you weren't going to come.

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:38.300
But now we can begin fifth period
exactly as planned!

00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:42.770
How stupid are you? It's all over.
There never was any gas, was there?

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:46.900
Fifth period will prove it
when it begins in a minute!

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:49.770
I'll make it a fun after-school activity!

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:50.860
Blue!

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:52.520
Drop the birdcage!

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:55.190
It's about damn time!

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:57.190
The wagtails are flying.

00:17:10.540 --> 00:17:12.330
HQ! Come in!

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:14.590
This is the front entrance! HQ!

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:18.050
It's no use, it won't open.

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:20.720
No luck over here, either!

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:23.980
This one won't open, either.

00:17:24.590 --> 00:17:27.430
Mario, every way in and out
has been sealed off.

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:29.890
We're completely locked in.

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:32.190
What's your game?

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:36.150
We have control of the hotel's systems!

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:38.910
You can't get out of here!

00:17:40.230 --> 00:17:41.100
Kaela?

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:41.870
He's right.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:44.330
I can't access the building's systems!

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:46.290
I'm being repelled!

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:50.000
The wagtails have all been caught!

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:53.620
We've rigged this building
with poison gas!

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:58.930
Enough to kill not only everyone here,
but everyone in the whole city!

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:04.090
The instant the clock strikes 9:00,
your lives will end!

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:08.930
If you want me to disable it,
someone here will have to...

00:18:09.300 --> 00:18:12.020
kill the mayor standing right there!

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:16.150
Do that, and the device will stop.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:22.650
If you don't believe me, fine.

00:18:22.650 --> 00:18:25.040
Come 9:00, you'll know for sure.

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:28.240
And then, everyone will end up like this!

00:18:30.490 --> 00:18:35.750
No fair, let me be part... of the plan.

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:38.090
Let me...

00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:47.140
Everyone, please remain calm!

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:49.060
No pushing, I said!

00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:53.360
Hey, who just felt me up?
You're under arrest!

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:55.560
You'll die, too!

00:18:56.100 --> 00:18:58.320
Kill the mayor yourself, then!

00:18:58.690 --> 00:19:01.650
Do that and it will save everyone!

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:04.280
You're a nutjob.

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:09.790
Listen, everyone here will die,
me included! An epic tragedy!

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:13.960
Tonight will be spoken of with terror
for all time!

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:19.720
But the names of you victims will crumble
into dust and fade away into oblivion!

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:23.720
In other words, the only name
future generations will remember

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:25.380
will be mine, the attacker!

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.300
Only mine!

00:19:29.260 --> 00:19:30.690
Why, you...

00:19:30.970 --> 00:19:35.150
Before long, my name will race around
the wilderness that is information

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:36.610
and become a legend!

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:39.570
How's this sound as the headline?

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:43.360
"A Young Boy's Beautiful Despair"?

00:19:44.110 --> 00:19:45.910
You psycho freak.

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:49.370
Does that make you angry,
Mr. Nameless Detective?

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:51.870
All for a pathetic notion like that?

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:57.040
That pathetic notion is going to beat you!
I feel sorry for you! Who are you?

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:02.300
I'll make sure everyone remembers.
Your stupid face and name!

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:06.680
As a dumbass criminal who was a failure!

00:20:07.090 --> 00:20:08.010
Kaela!

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:11.730
I was listening!
I'm pissed, too, so be quiet for a bit!

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.730
Cocky punks piss me off
worse than cockroaches!

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:18.190
Punks who do nothing
but whine about society piss me off!

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:19.230
-Besides--
-Kaela.

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:21.110
I said shut up!

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:24.200
Fine, whatever.

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:28.160
Sounds like you guys
made our big sister angry.

00:20:28.820 --> 00:20:30.570
Don't come crying to me.

00:20:31.740 --> 00:20:35.630
This is more complex than I thought.
They're not so dumb after all?

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:38.750
But that doesn't mean they're smart.

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:56.220
So you came after all.

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:02.980
Bull's-eye, and right on the money.

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:06.450
I wasn't expecting you to swallow
that cheap bait so easily.

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:09.570
Maybe that person is amazing after all.

00:21:09.570 --> 00:21:13.030
Right, you don't know who I mean
by "that person," do you?

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:16.620
Are you curious?
You're curious, aren't you?

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:19.750
But I won't tell you just yet.

00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:24.670
I would take you to them
if you agreed to come willingly,

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:27.130
but that's not what you want, is it?

00:21:29.210 --> 00:21:31.130
Oh, I'm so scared!

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:36.640
Are you planning to use that
to destroy me like you did Quinn?

00:21:38.220 --> 00:21:39.940
Quinn died,

00:21:40.560 --> 00:21:42.480
but I don't think I will.

00:21:43.060 --> 00:21:46.910
I'm kinda fast. Just a little bit.

00:21:48.020 --> 00:21:50.410
What we need is you.

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:53.200
But not your life.

00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:57.120
Do you understand what this means?

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:09.720
Who are you?

00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:29.400
Someday I’ll be gone

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:38.000
To somewhere that we belong

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:43.380
And god has never played his role

00:22:43.380 --> 00:22:47.670
Because I’m the one who saves my soul

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:52.800
It is a perfect world we’re longing for

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:55.930
So long...

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:26.590
Cursed shadows haunt and gather

00:23:26.590 --> 00:23:30.220
In the city of no answer

00:23:30.590 --> 00:23:34.510
as we follow endless questions

00:23:34.510 --> 00:23:38.430
hands up in the same reflection

00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:42.350
just used to be
Sometimes we try to feel how things

00:23:42.350 --> 00:23:46.480
just used to be

00:23:46.770 --> 00:23:50.570
No one ever make it better, no one ever lives forever

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:53.950
Wake me up and let me go

00:23:54.360 --> 00:24:02.160
Someday I’ll be gone

00:24:02.160 --> 00:24:08.250
To somewhere we all belong

00:24:08.250 --> 00:24:11.010
For so long
